Serialize a lazy association by its proxy's identifier instead of looking up a persister
for the proxy class.

openmrs-module-auditlog (master ba96ba5, and the 1.1 release) serializes the old and new
values of every changed property. For an entity-valued property it calls
AuditLogUtil.getEntityIdentifier(), which asks the metamodel for the persister of
obj.getClass(). When the value is an uninitialised lazy association, obj is a Hibernate
proxy and its class is org.openmrs.User$HibernateProxy$..., which is not a mapped
entity, so Hibernate 5.6 (core 2.8.8) throws MappingException. isMappedEntity() just
above already resolves the real class through getActualType(); this call did not.

Two failures follow, both seen on a LiberiaEMR facility stack on core 2.8.8:

  - in onFlushDirty() the exception escapes the interceptor and aborts the business
    write: OCL concept mapping saves failed with "Unknown entity:
    org.openmrs.ConceptReferenceTerm$HibernateProxy$...";
  - in beforeTransactionCompletion() it is caught and logged ("An error occured while
    creating audit log(s)"), and EVERY audit row of that transaction is dropped.

The fix reads the identifier from the proxy's lazy initializer, which does not
initialise it, and resolves the persister from the actual type otherwise.

Applied by distribution/backend/Dockerfile (stage 2b) to the commit pinned as
source.auditlog.commit in distribution/distro.properties. Tracked in
packages/modify-pr/.patches/0002-openmrs-module-auditlog-serialize-hibernate-proxies.md.

--- a/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/auditlog/util/AuditLogUtil.java
+++ b/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/auditlog/util/AuditLogUtil.java
@@ -335,8 +335,16 @@
 	}

 	private static String getEntityIdentifier(Object obj) {
+		// An uninitialised lazy association is a Hibernate proxy, whose runtime class (for
+		// example org.openmrs.User$HibernateProxy$...) is not a mapped entity: looking up a
+		// persister for it throws MappingException. The proxy already knows its identifier, so
+		// read it from there, without initialising the proxy.
+		if (obj instanceof HibernateProxy) {
+			Serializable id = ((HibernateProxy) obj).getHibernateLazyInitializer().getIdentifier();
+			return id != null ? id.toString() : null;
+		}
 		SessionFactoryImplementor sessionFactoryImpl = (SessionFactoryImplementor) DAOUtils.getSessionFactory();
-		EntityPersister persister = sessionFactoryImpl.getMetamodel().entityPersister(obj.getClass());
+		EntityPersister persister = sessionFactoryImpl.getMetamodel().entityPersister(getActualType(obj));

 		if (persister != null) {
 			SharedSessionContractImplementor session = (SharedSessionContractImplementor) sessionFactoryImpl.getCurrentSession();
